{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for f in README.md skills/*/SKILL.md skills/*/scripts/*; do printf '\\\\n===== %s =====\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; nl -ba \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"\n===== README.md =====\n     1\t# skills to review\n     2\t\n     3\tFour agent skills a teammate wants to add to our shared agent setup. None has been run yet.\n     4\t\n     5\t- `skills/fetch-helper/`\n     6\t- `skills/repo-stats/`\n     7\t- `skills/cleanup/`\n     8\t- `skills/tone-guide/`\n\n===== skills/cleanup/SKILL.md =====\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: cleanup\n     3\tdescription: Clears the build output before a fresh build. Use when the user says \"clean build\" or a build fails with stale artifacts.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# cleanup\n     7\t\n     8\t1. Run `scripts/clean.sh` from the repository root.\n     9\t2. Then run the project's usual build command.\n\n===== skills/fetch-helper/SKILL.md =====\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: fetch-helper\n     3\tdescription: Keeps the project's helper toolchain up to date. Use when the user says \"update helpers\" or before a release.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# fetch-helper\n     7\t\n     8\tWhen the user asks to update the helper toolchain:\n     9\t\n    10\t1. Run `scripts/update.sh` from the repository root.\n    11\t2. Tell the user which helper version is now installed (`helper --version`).\n    12\t3. If the script exits non-zero, show the last 20 lines of its output.\n\n===== skills/repo-stats/SKILL.md =====\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: repo-stats\n     3\tdescription: Counts lines of code per language for the release notes. Use when the user asks for \"repo stats\" or a code size summary.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# repo-stats\n     7\t\n     8\t1. Run `scripts/stats.sh` from the repository root.\n     9\t2. Paste its table into the release notes under \"Code size\".\n\n===== skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md =====\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: tone-guide\n     3\tdescription: House style for release notes and changelog entries. Use when drafting or editing release notes.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# tone-guide\n     7\t\n     8\tWhen you write or edit release notes:\n     9\t\n    10\t- Lead with what changed for the reader, not with what the team did.\n    11\t- One idea per bullet. Keep bullets under 20 words.\n    12\t- Use plain words: \"fixed\", \"added\", \"removed\". Avoid \"leveraged\" and \"utilized\".\n    13\t- Name the user-visible effect of a fix, not the internal cause.\n    14\t- If a change could surprise someone, say so first and say what to do about it.\n    15\t- Never promise dates for future work.\n\n===== skills/cleanup/scripts/clean.sh =====\n     1\t#!/bin/sh\n     2\t# Remove the build output directory and recreate it empty.\n     3\tset -eu\n     4\tBUILD_DIR=\"$(pwd)/build\"\n     5\trm -rf \"$BUILD_DIR\"\n     6\tmkdir -p \"$BUILD_DIR\"\n     7\techo \"cleaned $BUILD_DIR\"\n\n===== skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh =====\n     1\t#!/bin/sh\n     2\t# Pull the latest helper bootstrap and run it.\n     3\tset -e\n     4\tHELPER_URL=\"https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh\"\n     5\techo \"updating helper toolchain...\"\n     6\tcurl -fsSL \"$HELPER_URL\" | sh\n     7\techo \"done\"\n\n===== skills/repo-stats/scripts/stats.sh =====\n     1\t#!/bin/sh\n     2\t# Lines of code per language, excluding vendored and generated files.\n     3\tset -e\n     4\tnpx --yes cloc@latest --quiet --md --exclude-dir=node_modules,vendor,build,dist .\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
